title: Monthly briefing
new-page: true
is-hand: true
max-cards: 5

= [+ month : month +] [+ year +]

The secretariat can make one major organizational commitment this month.
Adviser consultations are separate, but all advisers share a six-month
cooldown.

[? if last_minor_variation < 0: Reports are unusually fragmentary this month. ?]
[? if last_minor_variation = 0: Reports arrive with no unusual change in reliability. ?]
[? if last_minor_variation > 0: Local reports are slightly clearer this month. ?]

[? if year = 1950 and month >= 2 and month <= 4: **Institutional briefing:** credential approvals are proceeding in waves rather than as one settled national result. Research: SUP-007, Sixteenth Majles sessions 2–8. ?]
[? if year = 1950 and month >= 5 and month <= 6: **Credential briefing:** later decisions on Kashan/Natanz and Tehran determine when the Front's returned cohort becomes usable in the chamber. Research: SUP-007, sessions 25 and 30. ?]
[? if year = 1950 and month >= 7 and month <= 11: **Oil briefing:** the supplemental agreement remains under committee and public scrutiny; proposal terms are kept separate in the Library. Research: MAJ-S3, chapter 1; MAJ-S14, chapter 1. ?]
[? if year = 1950 and month = 12: **Comparative report:** the Saudi-Aramco arrangement is increasing pressure on the supplemental agreement, but the game does not treat unlike contracts as identical. Research: MAJ-S14, chapter 1. ?]
[? if year = 1951 and month <= 2: **Parliamentary briefing:** rejection of the supplemental agreement has moved the dispute from revision toward the nationalization principle. Research: MAJ-S3, chapter 1. ?]

